1 NAME Moses Aron /Nathan/
2 GIVN Moses Aron
2 SURN Nathan
2 _MARNM Henriques
2 NICK Mausche Nasche
1 SEX M
1 BIRT
2 DATE 1690
2 ADDR
3 CITY Altona
3 STAE Schleswig-Holstein
3 CTRY Germany (Deutschland)
1 DEAT
2 DATE JUN 1744
2 ADDR
3 CITY Nakskov
3 STAE Lolland
3 CTRY Danmark
1 OCCU Købmand i Nakskov
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} http://jewmus.dk/klik-og-find/nakskov-synagoge/
2 CONT
2 CONT *
2 CONT
2 CONT https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henriques_(sl%C3%A6gt)
2 CONT
2 CONT *
2 CONT
2 CONT Translation of the below:
2 CONT Merchant. Immigrated to Nakskov from Glückstadt in 1711. His sons adopted their grandmother's name, Henriques.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Source: Berg, Sigurd: Fini Henriques – Living Music. Povl Branners Forlag. Copenhagen 1943. Page 7.]
2 CONT
2 CONT "In the year 1684, Jews were granted permission to settle in certain provincial towns in Denmark, including Nakskov, and it is from this town that the Henriques family originates. However, the first specific year recorded is 1725 
2 CONC when Pinches Henriques was born. His father, Mausche Nasche (Nasche means Nakskov), had five sons, namely Bendix (Pinches), Hertz, Aron, Berndt, and Ruben (father of Moses Ber)."
2 CONT
2 CONT [Source: Henriques, Ernst: The Henriques Family Tree. Copenhagen. Printed by O. C. Olsen & Co. 1903. Page 1.]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Since the Portuguese Jews in the Danish kingdoms enjoyed special privileges over the so-called German Jews, Moses Aron Nathan later claimed these privileges for his descendants, who adopted their Portuguese grandmother's name, He
2 CONC nriques, which was both her maiden name and her married name in her second marriage to her cousin, Moses Josua Henriques."
2 CONT
2 CONT
2 CONT .1.2.1.8.1.2.1  Moses Aron Nathan Henriques/Aron/Moses Aron Moses/Nathan / “Mausche Nasche” 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1690, Altona (nær Hamburg), Danmark (nu Tyskland)
2 CONT
2 CONT † Juni 1744, Nakskov
2 CONT
2 CONT Købmand. Indvandrede 1711 til Nakskov fra Glückstadt. Sønnerne antog Bedstemoderens Navn Henriques.
2 CONT
2 CONT [Kilde: Berg, Sigurd: Fini Henriques – Levende Musik. Povl Branners Forlag. København 1943. Side 7.]
2 CONT
2 CONT "I Aaret 1684 fik Jøder Tilladelse til at bosætte sig i enkelte Provinsbyer i Danmark, hvoriblandt Nakskov, og det er fra denne By at Familien Henriques stammer. Et bestemt Aarstal haves imidlertid først 1725, da Pinches Henriques
2 CONC  blev født. Hans Fader Mausche Nasche (Nasche betyder Nakskov) havde fem Sønner, nemlig Bendix (Pinches), Hertz, Aron, Berndt og Ruben (Fader til Moses Ber).
2 CONT
2 CONT [Kilde: Henriques, Ernst: Stamtavlen Henriques. Kjøbenhavn. Trykt hos O. C. Olsen & Co. 1903. Side 1.]
2 CONT
2 CONT "Da de portugisiske Jøder i de danske Riger nød særlige Forrettigheder fremfor de saakaldte tyske Jøder, gjorde Moses Aron Nathan senere Krav paa disse Særprivilegier for sine Efterkommere, som antog deres portugisiske Bedstemoder
2 CONC s Navn Henriques, hvilket baade var hendes Pigenavn og hendes Giftenavn i hendes andet Ægteskab med Fætteren Moses Josua Henriques."
2 CONT
2 CONT ~ Esther Cantor (/Esther Canvor), 1712 
2 CONT
2 CONT * 1690 (/1692) 
2 CONT
2 CONT † 1715 (/1716), Nakskov
2 CONT
2 CONT *  https://da.wikipedia.org/wiki/Henriques_(sl%C3%A6gt)
2 CONT * 
2 CONT
2 CONT http://jewmus.dk/klik-og-find/nakskov-synagoge/
2 CONT * 
