1 NOTE {geni:about_me} "In the year 1684, Jews were given permission to settle in some provincial towns in Denmark, including Nakskov, and it is from this town that the Henriques family originates. However, a specific year is not availab
2 CONC le until 1725, when Pinches Henriques was born. His father Mausche Nasche ( Nasche means Nakskov) had five sons, namely Bendix (Pinches), Hertz, Aron, Berndt and Ruben (father of Moses Ber).
2 CONT
2 CONT [Source: Henriques, Ernst: Pedigree Henriques. Copenhagen. Printed at O. C. Olsen & Co. 1903. Page 1.]
2 CONT
2 CONT "As the Portuguese Jews in the Danish kingdoms enjoyed special privileges over the so-called German Jews, Moses Aron Nathan [son of the Esther in this profile] later claimed these special privileges for his descendants, who adopte
2 CONC d their Portuguese grandmother's name of Henriques, which was both her maiden name and her married name in her second Marriage to Cousin Moses Josua Henriques."
2 CONT
2 CONT So, according to the above, Esther should be the daughter of Ruben Henriques rather than a Furst., but since I have no knowledge of whether Ruben Henriques may also have been known as Furst I am leaving both names there for other 
2 CONC managers to decide whether Furst is a surname connected with Ruben Henriques (23 FEB 2023)
