1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Ole Anton Owren was a Judge in Molde and apparently was way up there in Social Status.
2 CONT
2 CONT Social Status in Norway in the 1800's What was the social setting in Norway in the early 1800's?
2 CONT
2 CONT Lowest: Beggars, menial laborers, many were orphans or illegitimate or both. Hardly Better: The "good-for-nothing" Danish or Swedish soldiers stationed in Norway. Next: Servants hired out at age 15 or younger. Next: Husmenn and fa
2 CONC milies (provided contract help on a farm). Next: Craftsmen such as shoemakers, smiths, stonemasons, carpenters. Next: Foderaad couples (who had turned over the farm to others), widows. Next: Farm 'users' who were leasing small far
2 CONC ms from the owners. Next: Bonder, who's families owned their farms forever. Next: School teachers, priests, civil officers. Next: Nobility who were still largely Danish since Black Death times. Next: Danish (later Swedish) royalty
2 CONC  governing Norway.
2 CONT
2 CONT http://www.valdressamband.org/archive/social.html
