1 OCCU Lagmann på Færøyene, Amtmann i Finmarkens Amt, Stiftamtmand, Generalpostdirektør
1 NOTE {geni:about_me} Thorkild Jonsson Fjeldsted
2 CONT
2 CONT https://is.wikipedia.org/wiki/%C3%9Eorkell_Fjeldsted 
2 CONT
2 CONT From Wikipedia, the free Encyclopedia: Thorkild Jonsson Fjeldsted (1740 – 19 November 1796) (Icelandic name Þorkell Jónsson Fjeldsted) Icelandic lawyer, practised law in Copenhagen from 1763 to 1769, and from 1769 to 1772, he was 
2 CONC Prime Minister of the Faroe Islands. After that, he moved to Norway. From 1771 he was county governor of Finmarkens amt, then county governor of Bornholm and from 1780 of Christianssand amt. In 1786 he became a county governor of 
2 CONC Trondheim amt. He died in Copenhagen. [edit]References
2 CONT
2 CONT Løgtingið 150 - Hátíðarrit. Tórshavn 2002, Bind 2, S. 366. (Avsnitt Føroya løgmenn fram til 1816)
2 CONT
2 CONT Lagrettemann I Oppdal under takseringsforretningen etter storflommen [http://drivdalen.no/historie/historie-filer/storofsen.htm "Storofsen"] i 1790
2 CONT
2 CONT --------------------
2 CONT
2 CONT Amtmann på Færøyene 1769 til 1772
2 CONT
2 CONT Amtmann i Finnmark 1771 til 1778
2 CONT
2 CONT Stiftsamtmann i Trondheim 1779 - ca 1796
2 CONT
2 CONT ~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~~
